  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Why two stores",
      "items": [
        "add_episode writes into the org/project/user group; the index row is committed before the reply",
        "A page number needs a total; the graph has two episodes for every shared memory and no offset. The index has one row.",
        "Promotion copies the episode into the team group and adds team_episode_uuid to the same row."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Every read is scoped",
      "items": [
        "readable_groups = the team's group + your own. A third person's private memory cannot come back.",
        "Proven against real Neo4j on all three read paths — recent, fulltext, facts (make test-e2e)",
        "Discover reads recurring topic keys from the graph and checks the skills catalogue in Postgres for gaps"
      ]
    }
  ]
